# wallhack

> **wallhack** (plural **wallhacks**)
>
> *(video games)* A patch enabling a player to cheat by modifying the properties of walls, as by making them transparent or nonsolid.

A Layer 3 tunneling tool built for network pivoting in penetration testing scenarios.

A single 4 MB binary with no dependencies provides throughput and operational control via a built-in REPL and REST API on every entry node.

A full TUN interface on the [entry node](/concepts) routes all traffic to the target network transparently — TCP, UDP, ICMP, any protocol — without proxy chains or SOCKS configuration.

## Key Features

{% featurelist title="Core Capabilities" items=[
  "Transparent Layer 3 tunneling (all protocols)",
  "Multi-hop pivoting via intermediate relays",
  "High-performance QUIC and WebSockets transports",
  "Zero-config mTLS and E2EE (on by default)",
  "Interactive REPL and REST API for live management",
  "Zero-dependency static binaries (6 MB)"
] icon="check" /%}

## Performance and Reliability

Both transports sustain multi-gigabit throughput. QUIC handles high packet loss with per-stream recovery — a dropped packet stalls only that connection, not the entire tunnel.

{% grid %}
{% card title="UDP (QUIC)" icon="wifi" %}
- **Single stream:** 2.4 Gbps
- **4 streams:** 2.4 Gbps
- **Reverse:** 581 Mbps
- **4 streams @ 2% loss:** 17 Mbps
{% /card %}
{% card title="TCP (WebSockets)" icon="plug" %}
- **Single stream:** 2.4 Gbps
- **4 streams:** 2.5 Gbps
- **Latency:** ~21% lower RTT
- **4 streams @ 2% loss:** 7.7 Mbps
{% /card %}
{% /grid %}

{% callout type="note" %}
Measured with both nodes on the same machine with no real network between them. See [Benchmarks](/benchmarks) for full results including performance under packet loss.
{% /callout %}

## Management and Mutual TLS

Every [entry node](/concepts) includes a built-in REPL and REST API for live tunnel management. Secure the entire infrastructure with mutual TLS authentication using X.509 certificates.

[REPL & API →](/management) | [Mutual TLS →](/mtls)

## Binary Size

Distributed as a single static binary. Use the slim build to strip out the REST API and REPL for constrained environments.

| Target | Default | Slim |
|--------|---------|------|
| Linux x64 (glibc) | 6.05 MB | 4.65 MB |
| Linux x64 (musl, static) | 6.01 MB | 4.63 MB |
| Linux arm64 | 5.34 MB | 4.07 MB |

